id: pm-vcs-qfku
title: Remove vulnerable optional glob dependencies from the fleet duplication gate
description: "The pinned pm-ops 2026.10.6 duplication module imports its optional fast-glob 3.3.3 peer. Enabling the canonical gate installs braces 3.0.3 via micromatch; npm audit reports GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm with four high-severity development dependency entries (braces, micromatch, fast-glob, pm-ops). Production audit remains separate. pm-ops PR #163 proposes built-in fs.glob and jscpd 5 only; consume an approved published replacement in a dependency refresh, then regenerate the self-host bundle and rerun all release gates. Do not downgrade pm-ops or rewrite histories."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: dependencies,duplication,security
created_at: "2026-10-14T07:01:22.274Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T07:49:47.774Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
release: Unreleased
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T07:42:28.024Z",codex-agent,"Batch 3 addresses this existing dependency issue in the same PR as rollout Chore pm-vcs-3dxi. Use the published pm-ops 2026.10.14 implementation and remove the unused direct fast-glob peer; retain the pinned CLI, coverage inventory, thresholds and append-only histories. Regenerate the committed self-host bundle before HEAD verification."
  "2026-10-15T07:49:19.022Z",codex-agent,"Dependency remediation verified: exact pm-ops 2026.10.14 and removal of the unused fast-glob peer eliminate braces, fast-glob and micromatch from both full and production-only npm ls trees. Full npm audit --ignore-scripts now reports zero vulnerabilities versus the four high development findings at baseline. No SDK pin changed. Awaiting committed-head npm/Bun gates and self-host acceptance."
